course: dictionary
lesson: 4371
title: The word gymnast
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gymnast is a person who does gymnastics. Gymnastics is a sport of jumps, flips, balances and swinging on bars, rings, beams and mats. Gymnast is a noun, so it names a person.
explain: The context helps you. «Every body size can do sport: gymnast Simone Biles is about 1.42 m» tells you a gymnast is an athlete. «Gymnasts land on mats» tells you the sport includes flips and landings.
explain: Related words are gymnastics (the sport) and gym (a hall for exercise). Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Gymnasts land on mats» becomes «People who do gymnastics land on mats», and that still makes sense.
fact: A gymnast is a person who does gymnastics.
fact: Gymnastics is a sport of jumps, flips, balances and swinging on bars, rings, beams and mats.
fact: «Gymnast Simone Biles is about 1.42 m» shows that a short person can be a top athlete.
fact: «Gymnasts land on mats» because mats make a landing softer and safer.
fact: A gym is a hall for exercise, and gymnastics is the sport done there.
exercise: «Every body size can do sport: gymnast Simone Biles is about 1.42 m.» What is a gymnast? | A hall for exercise | *A person who does gymnastics | A machine that measures height | A type of mat
exercise: «Gymnasts land on mats.» Which word is related to gymnast? | airbag | mat | *gymnastics | chalk
exercise: Which place is a hall for exercise, where gymnasts might train? | *gym | helmet | airbag | chalk
test: «Climbers and gymnasts put chalk on their hands.» Why do they do this? | *Chalk soaks up sweat, so dry skin grips better | Chalk is a type of mat | Chalk makes their hands look clean for the judges | Chalk stops them feeling cold
test: Gymnastics is a sport of jumps, flips and balances. What do we call a person who does it? | Gym | Climber | *Gymnast | Helmet
exam: Gymnasts are strong, bendy and well balanced. Which words best describe a gymnast's body? | Slow and heavy | *Strong and bendy | Sleepy and soft | Loud and tall
